<title>JAPAN: Okinawa to host 1998 APEC energy meeting in Japan.</title>
<headline>Okinawa to host 1998 APEC energy meeting in Japan.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's southern island of Okinawa has been chosen as the site of next year's Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) forum's ministerial meeting to discuss energy policy, Japan's Trade Ministry said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The 18-member APEC meeting is to be held in October 1998, the ministry said.</p>
<p>The APEC forum's 1997 energy gathering is scheduled to begin on August 27 in Edmonton, Canada.</p>
<p>APEC groups Australia, Brunei, Canada, Chile, China, Hong Kong, Indonesia, Japan, Malaysia, Mexico, New Zealand, Papua New Guinea, the Philippines, Singapore, South Korea, Taiwan, Thailand and the United States.</p>
